{"name":"Wine Country","hex":"#602234","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"},{"term":"country","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The territory of a nation; a sovereign state or a region once independent and still distinct in institutions, language, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A large area regarded as distinct from other areas, e.g. because it is inhabited by a specific group of people"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["From or in the countryside, connected with it, or typical of it.","Of or connected to country music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/country"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine Country","blocks":[{"text":"Wine Country is a region of California, in the northern San Francisco Bay Area, known worldwide as a premier wine-growing region. The region is famed for its wineries, its cuisine, Michelin star restaurants, boutique hotels, luxury resorts, historic architecture, and culture. Viticulture and wine-making have been practiced in the region since the Spanish missionaries from Mission San Francisco Solano established the first vineyards in 1812."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Domaine_Carneros%2C_Napa_Valley%2C_CA_USA_-_panoramio_%289%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Domaine_Carneros%2C_Napa_Valley%2C_CA_USA_-_panoramio_%289%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_Country","wikidata":"Q1658318"},{"title":"Wine Country (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wine Country is a 2019 American comedy film co-produced and directed by Amy Poehler from a screenplay written by Emily Spivey and Liz Cackowski, based on a story conceived by Poehler, Spivey, and Cackowski. Starring Poehler, Maya Rudolph, Rachel Dratch, Ana Gasteyer, Paula Pell, Spivey, Jason Schwartzman, and Tina Fey, the film follows a group of longtime friends who take a vacation to Napa Valley as a birthday getaway. The film was released in select theaters on May 8, 2019, and digitally released for streaming on May 10, 2019, by Netflix."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Wine_Country.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_Country_(film)","wikidata":"Q55637796"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Country","blocks":[{"text":"A country is a political entity or its territory in the world. They function as sovereign states, unrecognized states, constituent countries, or dependent territories. A country may consist of multiple nations, a structure known as a multinational state. Countries are often distinguished as developing countries or developed countries. There is no universal agreement on the number of \"countries\" in the world. This ambiguity is a result of several countries not being recognized as sovereign states by the UN system, but are recognized by at least one UN member, known as \"diplomatic recognition\". These countries often have disputed territories and have only partial recognition. A number of entities without recognition are also commonly considered a country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg/330px-Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country","wikidata":"Q6256"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG/500px-Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG/1280px-Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG/500px-Castello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastello_di_Amorosa_courtyard_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg/500px-Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg/1280px-Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg/500px-Hop_Kiln_%28Walters_Ranch%29%2C_May_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHop_Kiln_(Walters_Ranch)%2C_May_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki